# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# Build context of infra/Dockerfile (docker build -f infra/Dockerfile ., Cloud Build, release.yml). The image
# needs the workspace manifests, the lockfile, the sources of frontend/, backend/ and packages/, LICENSE (the SPA
# build copies it into frontend/dist/licenses/), THIRD_PARTY.md and brand/ (the icon, and brand/LICENSE.md, which
# LICENSE points to for the gcportrait name and icon). Everything else stays out: smaller uploads,
# fewer cache misses, and nothing local (env files, credentials notes, build output) can reach an image layer.
# Patterns are anchored at the repository root; `**/` matches at any depth. .agents/ stays in: the catalog build
# reads the official asset-type list from .agents/skills/gcp-asset-catalog/references/.

# Version control, editors, assistants, OS noise
.git
.github
.claude
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Dependencies and build output: the image installs and builds its own
**/node_modules
**/.pnpm-store
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/.vite
**/.vite-demo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
out
packages/catalog/src/generated

# Local environment and credentials of any kind (backend/.env, *.local.* notes, keys)
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.local.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*-key.json
**/application_default_credentials.json
**/*.log

# Not part of the product: docs, release notes, deployment scripts
docs
infra/*
!infra/Dockerfile
**/*.md
!THIRD_PARTY.md
!brand/LICENSE.md

# The e2e workspace: only its manifest, which the lockfile's importers need
e2e/*
!e2e/package.json
